{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SkewSYTMaxCorner","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SkewSYTMaxCorner","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramCorner"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewInsertMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewInsertMax","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L232-L315","doc":"**Insert the maximal entry at a corner outside `inner`** — the mirror of the erase step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.not_mem_below_of_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.not_mem_below_of_corner","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L226-L230","doc":"Likewise strictly below it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.not_mem_right_of_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.not_mem_right_of_corner","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L220-L224","doc":"`(p, q)` being a corner rules out any cell strictly to its right in `outer`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.entry_lt_of_skew","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.entry_lt_of_skew","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L211-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.entry_lt_card_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.entry_lt_card_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L185-L196","doc":"Off the skew region every entry is `0`, so a positive bound holds there too.  Needed\nbecause the insert step must bound `S.entry` at cells it knows nothing about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mem_eraseCorner_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mem_eraseCorner_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L180-L183","doc":"A cell of `outer` other than the deleted corner survives the deletion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.card_skewCellsOf_eraseCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.card_skewCellsOf_eraseCorner","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L166-L173","doc":"So the skew size drops by exactly one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewCellsOf_eraseCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewCellsOf_eraseCorner","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L151-L164","doc":"Deleting that corner removes exactly it from the skew region.\n\nNote this needs **no** hypothesis that `c ∉ inner` — set-difference-minus-a-cell is\n`erase` on the difference either way.  (The unused binder was there until the linter\npointed out it does no work; carrying it would have implied the identity depends on the\ncorner being outside `inner`, which it does not.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.le_eraseCorner_of_notMem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.le_eraseCorner_of_notMem","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L143-L149","doc":"Deleting a corner that lies outside `inner` keeps `inner` inside the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.exists_max_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.exists_max_corner","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L106-L136","doc":"**The maximal entry sits on a removable corner of `outer` that is outside `inner`.**\n\nThis is the erase-max step of the skew branching rule, and the one place its geometry\ndiffers from the straight case: the corner must additionally be shown to lie outside\n`inner`, which is exactly what makes `outer ∖ c` still contain `inner`.\n\nBoth neighbours are ruled out the same way — if the neighbour were in `outer` it would be\na *skew* cell (`skew_right_mem` / `skew_down_mem`), its entry would strictly exceed the\nmaximum by `row_strict` / `col_strict`, and yet be bounded by it via `skew_mem_range`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_down_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_down_mem","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L99-L104","doc":"The downward neighbour, likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_right_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_right_mem","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L91-L97","doc":"A skew cell's right neighbour, if in `outer`, is also a skew cell: it cannot be in\n`inner`, since `inner` is a lower set and the original cell is not in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_exists_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_exists_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L82-L89","doc":"**Every value below `|skew|` is attained.**  The surjective half of the same\n`content` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_mem_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_mem_range","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L73-L80","doc":"**The entries on the skew region are exactly `0, …, |skew| − 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L59-L71","doc":"**The entry map is injective on the skew region.**  `content` says the image is\n`range |skew|`, and a set whose image has the same cardinality as itself is mapped\ninjectively.  Every step of a skew insert/erase construction needs this, and unlike the\nstraight case — where `StandardYoungTableau.bijOn` hands it over directly — it has to be\nderived from the image equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewCellsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewCellsOf","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewSYTMaxCorner.lean#L55-L57","doc":"The skew cells of `outer / inner`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}